{'review': '{\n  "review": "<<<ARTIFACT review_report>>>\\n{\\n  \\"overall_status\\": \\"NEEDS_FIXES\\",\\n  \\"quality_score\\": 6.0,\\n  \\"summary\\": {\\n    \\"critical\\": 0,\\n    \\"high\\": 0,\\n    \\"medium\\": 3,\\n    \\"low\\": 2,\\n    \\"passed_checks\\": [\\"Type annotations present\\", \\"Effect cleanup implemented\\", \\"No hardcoded secrets in code\\"]\\n  },\\n  \\"findings\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-001\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"medium\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"security\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"Access token placed in URL query string without encoding\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [43, 43],\\n      \\"description\\": \\"The access token is appended directly to the URL as a query parameter without using encodeURIComponent. This can break the URL if the token contains special characters and may lead to injection or malformed requests.\\",\\n      \\"impact\\": \\"Malformed WebSocket URL causing connection failures; potential security issues if token includes characters that alter URL interpretation.\\",\\n      \\"suggested_fix\\": \\"Encode the token and safely append query parameters using the URL API.\\",\\n      \\"code_before\\": \\"    const wsUrlWithToken = \\\\`${url}?access_token=${accessToken}\\\\`;\\",\\n      \\"code_after\\": \\"    const urlObj = new URL(url);\\\\n    urlObj.searchParams.set(\'access_token\', accessToken);\\\\n    const wsUrlWithToken = urlObj.toString();\\",\\n      \\"references\\": [\\"OWASP A1:2021 - Injection\\", \\"CWE-89\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-002\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"low\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"Logging URL with access token may expose sensitive data\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [44, 44],\\n      \\"description\\": \\"The connection log includes the full URL with the access token as a query parameter. If logs are stored insecurely or exposed, the token could be leaked.\\",\\n      \\"impact\\": \\"Token leakage via logs, potentially leading to session hijacking if logs are accessed by unauthorized parties.\\",\\n      \\"suggested_fix\\": \\"Avoid logging the full URL; log only the base URL or a masked version.\\",\\n      \\"code_before\\": \\"    console.log(`Attempting to connect to WebSocket: ${wsUrlWithToken}`);\\",\\n      \\"code_after\\": \\"    console.log(`Attempting to connect to WebSocket: ${url}`);\\",\\n      \\"references\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-003\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"medium\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"WebSocket reference not cleaned up on close/error\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [59, 74],\\n      \\"description\\": \\"The `ws.current` reference is never set to `null` after the WebSocket closes or errors. This can leave a stale reference to a closed WebSocket object, which may cause confusion if inspected.\\",\\n      \\"impact\\": \\"Stale reference may lead to incorrect checks (e.g., `ws.current` appears truthy but socket is closed) and potential memory leaks if listeners are not released.\\",\\n      \\"suggested_fix\\": \\"Set `ws.current = null` in the `onclose` and `onerror` handlers after cleanup.\\",\\n      \\"code_before\\": \\"    ws.current.onerror = (event) => {\\\\n      console.error(\\\\\\"WebSocket error:\\\\\\", event);\\\\n      onError?.(event);\\\\n    };\\\\n\\\\n    ws.current.onclose = (event) => {\\\\n      console.log(\\\\\\"WebSocket disconnected:\\\\\\", event.code, event.reason);\\\\n      setIsConnected(false);\\\\n      onClose?.(event);\\\\n\\\\n      if (!event.wasClean && reconnectAttempts.current < reconnectLimit) {\\\\n        reconnectAttempts.current++;\\\\n        console.log(`Attempting to reconnect in ${reconnectInterval / 1000}s... (Attempt ${reconnectAttempts.current}/${reconnectLimit})`);\\\\n        timeoutId.current = setTimeout(connect, reconnectInterval);\\\\n      }\\\\n    };\\\\n\\",\\n      \\"code_after\\": \\"    ws.current.onerror = (event) => {\\\\n      console.error(\\\\\\"WebSocket error:\\\\\\", event);\\\\n      onError?.(event);\\\\n      ws.current = null;\\\\n    };\\\\n\\\\n    ws.current.onclose = (event) => {\\\\n      console.log(\\\\\\"WebSocket disconnected:\\\\\\", event.code, event.reason);\\\\n      setIsConnected(false);\\\\n      onClose?.(event);\\\\n      ws.current = null;\\\\n\\\\n      if (!event.wasClean && reconnectAttempts.current < reconnectLimit) {\\\\n        reconnectAttempts.current++;\\\\n        console.log(`Attempting to reconnect in ${reconnectInterval / 1000}s... (Attempt ${reconnectAttempts.current}/${reconnectLimit})`);\\\\n        timeoutId.current = setTimeout(connect, reconnectInterval);\\\\n      }\\\\n    };\\\\n\\",\\n      \\"references\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-004\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"medium\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"useCallback dependencies on inline functions cause unnecessary reconnects\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [28, 76],\\n      \\"description\\": \\"The `connect` callback is memoized with dependencies `onOpen`, `onMessage`, `onError`, `onClose`. If any of these callback functions change (e.g., due to parent re-renders), a new `connect` function is created, triggering the `useEffect` to re-run and potentially causing disconnect/connect cycles.\\",\\n      \\"impact\\": \\"Unnecessary WebSocket disconnects and reconnects, increased latency, and potential loss of messages.\\",\\n      \\"suggested_fix\\": \\"Wrap the callback options in `useRef` or use `useCallback` for each handler separately, or remove them from the dependency array and use the refs inside `connect`.\\",\\n      \\"code_before\\": \\"  const connect = useCallback(() => {\\\\n    // ...\\\\n  }, [url, accessToken, onOpen, onMessage, onError, onClose, reconnectInterval, reconnectLimit]);\\\\n\\",\\n      \\"code_after\\": \\"  const onOpenRef = useRef(onOpen);\\\\n  const onMessageRef = useRef(onMessage);\\\\n  const onErrorRef = useRef(onError);\\\\n  const onCloseRef = useRef(onClose);\\\\n  useEffect(() => {\\\\n    onOpenRef.current = onOpen;\\\\n    onMessageRef.current = onMessage;\\\\n    onErrorRef.current = onError;\\\\n    onCloseRef.current = onClose;\\\\n  }, [onOpen, onMessage, onError, onClose]);\\\\n\\\\n  const connect = useCallback(() => {\\\\n    // ... same body but use onOpenRef.current etc.\\\\n  }, [url, accessToken, reconnectInterval, reconnectLimit]);\\\\n\\",\\n      \\"references\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-005\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"low\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"No validation of WebSocket URL format\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [28, 28],\\n      \\"description\\": \\"The `url` parameter is not validated to ensure it starts with `ws://` or `wss://`. An invalid URL will cause the WebSocket constructor to throw.\\",\\n      \\"impact\\": \\"Runtime error if an incorrect URL is passed, breaking the hook.\\",\\n      \\"suggested_fix\\": \\"Add a simple validation check at the start of `connect` (or in the hook) and warn/error if the URL does not match expected pattern.\\",\\n      \\"code_before\\": \\"  const connect = useCallback(() => {\\\\n    if (!accessToken) {\\\\n      console.warn(\\\\\\"No access token provided for WebSocket connection.\\\\\\");\\\\n      return;\\\\n    }\\\\n    // ...\\\\n  }, [...]);\\\\n\\",\\n      \\"code_after\\": \\"  const connect = useCallback(() => {\\\\n    if (!accessToken) {\\\\n      console.warn(\\\\\\"No access token provided for WebSocket connection.\\\\\\");\\\\n      return;\\\\n    }\\\\n    try {\\\\n      new URL(url); // throws if invalid\\\\n    } catch (e) {\\\\n      console.error(\\\\\\"Invalid WebSocket URL:\\\\\\", url);\\\\n      return;\\\\n    }\\\\n    // ...\\\\n  }, [...]);\\\\n\\",\\n      \\"references\\": []\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"positive_observations\\": [\\n    \\"Proper use of `useEffect` cleanup to close WebSocket and clear timeouts on unmount or token change\\",\\n    \\"Reconnection logic with attempt limits and exponential backoff-ready interval\\",\\n    \\"TypeScript interfaces provide good type safety for options and callbacks\\",\\n    \\"`sendMessage` correctly checks WebSocket ready state before sending\\",\\n    \\"Early return when no access token is provided, preventing unnecessary connection attempts\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n<<<ENDARTIFACT>>\\n"\n}'}